      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — named constants for the opaque surrogate-pair literal, cleaner variable names, comments explaining the *why* behind each expected outcome, and removing unused imports.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version extracts the opaque surrogate pair `\"\\uD835\\uDD59\"` into a named constant `DOUBLE_STRUCK_SMALL_H` with a clear Unicode annotation, renames variables to reflect which escape mode is under test, adds comments explaining *why* each expected output occurs, removes unused imports, and adds a class-level Javadoc summarising the overall test intent — all without changing any method calls, arguments, or expected values."
